**Fixes applied:**

| File | Bug | Fix |
|------|-----|-----|
| `job_queue.py:dequeue` | Race condition — multiple workers grabbed the same pending job via interleaved `await` | Added `asyncio.Lock`, wrapped iteration+assignment atomically; removed the erroneous `await asyncio.sleep(0.01)` |
| `worker.py:process_job` | Exception caught but `queue.fail()` never called — job left stuck in `processing` | Added `queue.fail(job["id"], str(e))` in the except block |
